Only hits: CSS `linear-gradient`/`radial-gradient` (purely visual glow decorations in `BackgroundAnimation.tsx`, `SlicingProgressModal.module.scss`, `SpaceTransitionOverlay.module.scss`, `Viewport3D.module.scss`), a slicing step label `'20-interpolation'` in `slicingSteps.ts`, prose comments about numeric interpolation in `gcodeLayer.ts` (nozzle/pivot math, arc math) and `Viewport3D.tsx` (float precision), and an unrelated `ControllerProps` name match in `ui/form.tsx`. **No `BABYLON.Color3.Lerp` usage anywhere in the repo, and no reusable colormap/gradient utility exists.** A "color by numeric value" feature would need a brand-new colormap helper (e.g. HSV/viridis-style value→Color3 mapping) built from scratch.

## 8. CategoriesSidebar / sibling components / props from `useGCodePreview`

Already covered in §4: `CategoriesSidebar.tsx` itself contains **no direct import** of `GCodeLineTypeLegend`/`GCodeSpeedSelector` — it's purely a layout shell with 4 slot props (`previewUpperContent`, `previewLowerHeader`, `previewLowerContent`, `previewBelowContent`), rendered at lines 690–726. The real composition (and thus the insertion point for a new selector) is in `pages/Index.tsx` lines 255–293, where `gcodePreview` (the return value of `useGCodePreview(active)`) is destructured to wire props into each mounted component: `fileInfo`, `lineVisibility`, `setLineVisible`, `speed`, `setSpeed`, `showFullHead`, `setShowFullHead`, `conversionSource`, `conversion`, `convert`, `setOffPlateHighlight`, `conversionAvailable` are all already available at that exact call site for a new "color by" control to consume/extend.

## 9. Slicer-comment regex parsing already present

In `gcodeLayer.ts`, `handleComment()` (lines 305–345) and its regexes:
- `FEATURE_RE = /^\s*(?:TYPE|FEATURE)\s*[:\s]\s*(.+?)\s*$/i` (line 145) — `;TYPE:`/`; FEATURE ` line-type markers, resolved via `resolveLineType()`.
- `WIPE_START_RE`/`WIPE_END_RE` (146–147) — `;WIPE_START`/`;WIPE_END`.
- `ICESL_LAYER_RE = /^\s*<\/?layer>\s*$/i` (148) — IceSL's `<layer>`/`</layer>` tags.
- `HEADER_RE = /^\s*([a-z][a-z0-9_.]*)\s*[:=]\s*(.*?)\s*$/i` (151) — generic `key: value` / `key = value` header parser, whose recognized keys (switch at lines 321–344) are: `printable_area`, `bed_shape`, `bed_size_x_mm`, `bed_size_y_mm`, `bed_circular`, `filament_diameter`, `filament_diameter_mm_0`, `filament_density`, `machine_max_speed_x`, `retraction_length`, `printer_model`, `printer`, `target_machine.name`, `apex_conversion_mode`.
- **Confirmed absent**: no `;WIDTH`, `;LAYER_HEIGHT`, `;MinZ`, `;flavor`, `;Z_HEIGHT`, or any other per-line/per-layer slicer metadata comment is parsed anywhere in `gcodeLayer.ts` or `gcodeGenerator.ts`. Any "color by layer height" or "color by line width" mode would need brand-new comment regexes added to `handleComment()` (e.g., Cura's `;LAYER_HEIGHT:x.xx`, PrusaSlicer/OrcaSlicer per-line `;WIDTH:x.xxxxx` / `;HEIGHT:x.xxxxx` comments before extrusion moves) — none of this parsing infrastructure exists today; only the generic header-line and `;TYPE:`/`;FEATURE:` feature-marker regimes are implemented, both fired only via `handleComment()` inside the main per-line loop (lines 410–418).
